# Accepted image risks, read by jay-withers/workflows' docker.yml. Each entry
# says why it does not apply here and expires, so it is looked at again.

# go-jose: denial of service when parsing a JWK set containing RSA keys.
# Compiled into Grafana's own binary (13.2.5 ships v4.1.4; fixed in 4.1.6),
# so only a Grafana release can fix it. Grafana parses JWKs only for JWT and
# OAuth sign-in, and both are off here: one local admin, no SSO. Drop this
# entry once a Grafana release bumps go-jose.
CVE-2026-116587 exp:2026-12-31

# golang.org/x/net/html: denial of service from crafted HTML input. Compiled
# into Grafana's own binary (13.2.5 ships v0.61.0) and its bundled Prometheus
# plugin (v0.60.0); fixed in 0.62.0, so only a Grafana release can fix it, and
# 13.2.5 is the newest 13.2. The Prometheus data source isn't configured here
# (Azure Monitor only), and the binary's HTML parsing sits behind the single
# admin login: the worst case is a crashed scale-to-zero replica. Short expiry,
# because it is reachable in principle: drop this entry once a Grafana release
# bumps x/net. Accepted by the user on 2026-11-06.
CVE-2026-78661 exp:2026-12-06
